  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Truly my soul waiteth upon God: from him cometh my salvation.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "He only is my rock and my salvation; he is my defence; I shall not be greatly moved.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "How long will ye imagine mischief against a man? ye shall be slain all of you: as a bowing wall shall ye be, and as a tottering fence.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "They only consult to cast him down from his excellency: they delight in lies: they bless with their mouth, but they curse inwardly. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "My soul, wait thou only upon God; for my expectation is from him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "He only is my rock and my salvation: he is my defence; I shall not be moved.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "In God is my salvation and my glory: the rock of my strength, and my refuge, is in God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Trust in him at all times; ye people, pour out your heart before him: God is a refuge for us. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Surely men of low degree are vanity, and men of high degree are a lie: to be laid in the balance, they are altogether lighter than vanity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Trust not in oppression, and become not vain in robbery: if riches increase, set not your heart upon them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "God hath spoken once; twice have I heard this; that power belongeth unto God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:62:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Also unto thee, O Lord, belongeth mercy: for thou renderest to every man according to his work.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 62:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:62:12"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
